    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization applied whenever an owner is created.\n\n**New class \u2014 `rest/validation/AddressNormalizer.java`:** a single-responsibility normalizer sitting alongside the existing `EmailNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer`. Its `normalize(String)`:\n- trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces,\n- upper-cases the result,\n- expands street-type abbreviations token-by-token (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`),\n- returns `\"\"` for `null`/blank input so a whitespace-only address becomes blank.\n\n**Wiring \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:** one line normalizes the DTO's address before anything else runs:\n```java\nownerFieldsDto.setAddress(AddressNormalizer.normalize(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress()));\n```\nPlacing it first means every downstream step naturally uses the normalized form with no duplication:\n- the existing `OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields` now sees the normalized value, so an address that is blank after normalization is rejected (400);\n- the mapped `Owner` is persisted and returned with the normalized address;\n- household duplicate detection (`findOwnersInHousehold`) and the shared household id (`HouseholdIdGenerator.generate`) both operate on the normalized `owner.getAddress()`.\n\nI left `updateOwner` and the V2 list controller untouched, since the spec scopes this to owner creation (`POST /api/owners`, served by V1).\n\nAll tests pass: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 covering whitespace/case (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`), abbreviation expansion (`\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`), and rejection of a blank-after-normalization address.",
